{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445015-do-you-ever-find-yourself-watching-vampire-movies-and-thinking-of-them-in-game-terms","id":1445015,"title":"Do you ever find yourself watching vampire movies and thinking of them in game-terms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T02:20:33-07:00","id":1445015,"title":"Do you ever find yourself watching vampire movies and thinking of them in game-terms?","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=busozfENY0I\" data-code=\"busozfENY0I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/busozfENY0I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I was rewatching &quot;Fright Night&quot; and had this series of thoughts:<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to intimate him to move aside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation+Intimidation&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls a Bestial Failure*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me', and his unbearable insolence causes you to gain the Harm Compulsion&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I bare my fangs, activate my Eyes of the Beast and Protean Claws, and do a called shot to his jugular with my claws&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-*mentally notes that activating both the eyes and claws should take two rounds, but lets it slide for Rule of Cool's sake* &quot;Roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls, scoring four 10's, and three 6's*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you land a devastating critical hit to his jugular. The bouncer goes down, mortally wounded. Another bouncer rushes in to help him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige player-&quot;I blood surge my Strength, pick him up by the throat, and throw him across the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige player rolls, scoring a messy critical&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you lift him by the throat, crushing his windpipe in the process, and hurl him across the room. Everyone on the dancefloor panics and rushes for the door. In the chaos, you lose track of Amy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-21-2021, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:42:34-07:00","id":1445028,"title":"","content":"I just finished watching tokyo vampire hotel which was something else .. but the entire time I kept thinking &quot;well those are gangrel claws&quot;. &quot;that was fortitude&quot; &quot;that was a tzimisce flesh rafting&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:55:35-07:00","id":1445030,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s hard *not* to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:58:07-07:00","id":1445047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445015-do-you-ever-find-yourself-watching-vampire-movies-and-thinking-of-them-in-game-terms?p=1445030#post1445030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s hard *not* to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Depending on the movie, I have the thoughts sometimes or constantly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T08:12:56-07:00","id":1445049,"title":"","content":"Nah, trying to put one box in another box ruins the enjoyment. Vampire movies existed before VTM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T08:26:02-07:00","id":1445052,"title":"","content":"Yes I do a lot, I think of all fictional vampires in masquerade terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:25:42-07:00","id":1445057,"title":"","content":"Though not VTM related I've always thought of Guardians of the Galaxy as the quintessential D&amp;D movie. A ragtag group of murder hobos who fit neatly into D&amp;D class archetypes.<br /> <br /> Starlord- Bard<br /> Gamora - Fighter/Rogue<br /> Drax - Barbarian<br /> Groot - Druid<br /> Rocket - Sorcerer <br /> <br /> Im sure I've done so with vampire movies as well. Interview is a bunch of Toreadors as an obvious example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:46:03-07:00","id":1445065,"title":"","content":"Not movies but Manhuas. Turned out one of them with My Idol is a Vampire whas heavility inspired from either VtM or VtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T11:19:49-07:00","id":1445081,"title":"","content":"When I saw the new Resident evil village trailer I couldn't help but think about vtm. Not just the vampire vibe but their powers being like disciplines. Fingers turning into claws and turning into a swarm of insects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25838-dart93","name":"Dart93","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}